Single-database configuration for Flask.

Schema bootstrap:

`000000000001_initial_production_schema.py` is the reviewed, frozen baseline for
an empty database. `flask db upgrade` creates the baseline and then follows the
linear delta history to the current single head. The baseline is immutable after
release; future model changes require a new forward revision.

Production and managed startup must use the migration coordinator. It probes the
current revision, refuses populated unversioned databases, requires a verified
coordinated backup before an approved destructive upgrade, runs Alembic with the
dedicated migration credential, and verifies the target revision before workers
or readiness can proceed. Automatic downgrade is not supported.

`db.create_all()` remains only as an explicitly enabled disposable development
and test escape hatch. It is not a production bootstrap, migration, or stamping
path. Never use `flask db stamp` to bypass schema validation.

Maintainers can reproduce a candidate baseline with
`scripts/generate_initial_schema_migration.py` for review, but must not overwrite
the committed baseline after release. Verify the chain with `flask db heads` and
the Phase 4 migration tests.
